{
  "id": "26850_kiokusuru",
  "headword": "{記憶|きおく}する",
  "reading": "きおくする",
  "romaji": "kiokusuru",
  "part_of_speech": "suru verb",
  "gloss": "to memorize; to remember; to commit to memory",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to memorize; to remember; to commit to memory",
      "explanation": "To store information in one's memory, either deliberately through study or naturally through experience. Also used for computers storing data."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "26850_kiokusuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{単語|たんご}を{記憶|きおく}する。",
      "english": "To memorize vocabulary.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26850_kiokusuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "あの{日|ひ}のことは{今|いま}でもはっきり{記憶|きおく}している。",
      "english": "I still clearly remember that day.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26850_kiokusuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{人間|にんげん}の{脳|のう}は{膨大|ぼうだい}な{量|りょう}の{情報|じょうほう}を{記憶|きおく}することができる。",
      "english": "The human brain can memorize an enormous amount of information.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26850_kiokusuru_ex4",
      "japanese": "パスワードをブラウザに{記憶|きおく}させると{便利|べんり}だが{危険|きけん}でもある。",
      "english": "Having the browser remember your password is convenient but also risky.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The noun {記憶|きおく} (memory) is extremely common and appears in everyday conversation, while the verb form {記憶|きおく}する is somewhat more formal than {覚|おぼ}える. Also used in computing contexts for data storage.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {記憶|きおく}{力|りょく}: memory (ability)\n- {記憶|きおく}に{残|のこ}る: to remain in memory\n- {記憶|きおく}が{薄|うす}れる: memory fades\n- {記憶|きおく}{喪失|そうしつ}: amnesia; memory loss\n- {記憶|きおく}{容量|ようりょう}: memory capacity (computing)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {覚|おぼ}える: to remember, to memorize — everyday term, less formal\n- {暗記|あんき}する: to memorize by heart — specifically rote memorization\n- {思|おも}い{出|だ}す: to recall — retrieving a memory, not storing one",
